[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67737,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Calcifying fibrous tumour is a rare, benign tumour occurring in visceral pleura, composed of paucicellular collagenized fibrous tissue with associated chronic inflammation and psammomatous and/or dystrophic calcification.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67738,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8817/0 Calcifying fibrous tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67739,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F01 &amp; XH7TH6 Benign neoplasm of intrathoracic organs &amp; Calcifying fibrous tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67740,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> calcifying fibrous pseudotumour; childhood fibrous tumour with psammoma bodies.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67741,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67742,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Calcifying fibrous tumour is typically limited to the pleura, although cases arising within lung parenchyma occur rarely {14645962}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67743,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "<p>Patients may be asymptomatic or may present with chest pain or non-productive cough.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Imaging studies show either a solitary or multiple pleural-based nodular masses. CT shows a well-defined pleural-based tumour (or tumours) with central areas of increased attenuation due to calcification. So-called disseminated (more likely multiple/multicentric) bilateral pleural lesions have been reported {18978573; 20621934; 31746679}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-25T18:08:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67744,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pleural calcifying fibrous tumours occur mainly in women, with a median age of 39&nbsp;years (range: 23&ndash;54&nbsp;years) {15660285; 8607443; 18978573; 29689243}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67745,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67746,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "<p>Deleterious mutations in <em>ZNF717</em>, <em>FRG1</em>, and <em>CDC27</em>, as well as tumour-specific copy-number losses, including a large (302&nbsp;kb) loss at 6p22.2&nbsp;&ndash; comprising 32&nbsp;genes of the histone cluster&nbsp;1 family and the hemochromatosis gene (<em>HFE</em>)&nbsp;&ndash; have been reported {29689243}, which may contribute to tumorigenesis. Rare familial cases have also been reported {12817428}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-11T14:13:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67747,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "<p>The tumours are well circumscribed, unencapsulated, solid, and firm, with a gritty texture. The average size is 50 mm (range: 15&ndash;125 mm).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-01T10:27:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67748,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These lesions are hypocellular, consisting of bland fibroblasts in a prominent collagenous stroma with a sparse lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate. There are usually dystrophic or psammomatous calcifications {8607443; 18978573; 29689243; 21850588}. By immunohistochemistry, the lesional cells may be CD34-positive, while BCL2, STAT6, &beta;-catenin, and ALK are negative. In the differential diagnosis, both inflammatory myofibroblastic tumour and solitary fibrous tumour are more cellular, the former being fascicular and the latter being patternless with branching, thin-walled vessels. Desmoid fibromatosis has ill-defined borders and lacks the characteristic dystrophic/psammomatous calcifications.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67749,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67750,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67751,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A well-defined, paucicellular, and collagenized pleural-based mass with associated psammomatous and/or dystrophic calcification</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67752,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67753,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Approximately 10&ndash;15% of lesions recur locally but not destructively. Local recurrence is not predictable on morphological grounds and is mainly due to incomplete resection. There is no potential for metastasis.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:09:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]